  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prepare, Protect, Promote: Empowering Young Civil Society Actors to defend freedoms of association and peaceful assembly</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;People in Need (PIN) and the European Partnership for Democracy (EPD) have designed an action to &lt;u&gt;prepare&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;protect&lt;/u&gt; young CSAs - formal civil society organisations, informal movements, individual activists, and social movements - to empower them to &lt;u&gt;promote&lt;/u&gt; the fundamental freedoms of association and assembly across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Action is rooted in its human rights-based approach that centres &lt;u&gt;young people&lt;/u&gt; at the heart of its programming, strengthening their capacities and potential for driving civic activism and promoting the fundamental FoAPA that underlie civic space. The capacity development and Financial Support to Third Parties (FSTP) &lt;u&gt;totalling over 543,000 EUR (18.5% of the total budget)&lt;/u&gt; will empower target youth-led and youth-focused CSAs to play a leading role in &lt;u&gt;protecting and promoting democracy, human rights and fundamental freedoms worldwide.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;u&gt;30-month Action will target between 50-60 youth-led and youth-focused CSAs&lt;/u&gt; from 10 countries for organisational and technical capacity development, funding, advocacy and networking opportunities. In addition, protection support will be available to &lt;u&gt;70-80 youth-led and youth-focused CSAs, working on FoAPA issues.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action will deliver research into methods of observing peaceful protests and monitoring violations of rights of association and assembly that will be used by CSAs and the international policymaking community for evidence-based advocacy. Finally, the Action delivers the priorities for networking and peer-to-peer learning by acting as a convener between the FFPA Lot 2 cohort to develop a global community of practice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 10 countries selected for capacity development and advocacy work are from three regions: Latin America (Cuba, Ecuador, El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras, Nicaragua, Venezuela), MENA (Tunisia) and Central Asia (Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
